    "turn_idx": 7,
    "turn_text": "You know, they were somewhat interested. I mean, they were immigrants, so they, you know, were more focused on keeping their head down to getting a house, making paying the bills. But my mom's father spent years in jail alongside Gandhi in the 1940s. in the 1930s as well in India's independence movement. And so she had grown up in India in a family that was pretty close to politics. And he was part of India's very, very first parliament. So I'm sure that had an influence at least on her. And I remember sometimes during dinner as a family we'd watch Peter Jennings or Tom Brokaw and they'd make some comments about it. They were not politically active, but I would say they were well informed about the news and what was going on.",
