    "turn_text": "I did, which was a very interesting Morris Arnold. He was a judge in Little Rock, Arkansas, and his brother was a judge too. He was more, more, I think it was slightly more conservative, but a great, a great judge in academic. And I got to spend a year in Little Rock, Arkansas. which for me was the first time really spending time down south. And I enjoyed my time there. It's what made me a fan of barbecue. I never really had barbecue before going down a little rock. And I also gave me an appreciation for Sort of the incredible diversity of the country. There was this like Indian American group in Little Rock, Arkansas that was doing all these things and would invite me into a different event. So this was back in the early 2000s. So I enjoyed the year there and Buzz Arnold just turned 80 and still I'm in touch with him.",
