  {
    "episode_id": 89151,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/9/89151.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 18,
    "turn_text": "All right, you did one of the hardest and in my judgment, loneliest things that someone can do, which is run against an incumbent. And I know how lonely it is from personal experience. I just wrote a book on making decisions. And so you had a decision to make. I'm sure there were people in your life saying, okay, Congressman, you have a bright future, but wait, just wait. Don't run this cycle. What led to your decision to challenge and incumbent, which is a very, very hard thing to do?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
