  {
    "episode_id": 89151,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/9/89151.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 21,
    "turn_text": "So it was about 10 years before I ran again, but I loved running. I mean, at the time, because I still, you know, you get to say what you believe. All these people, you know, one of the things that I find rather odd as people say, well, bro, how do you do it? How do you put up with being a member of Congress at this moment? And I say, look, we're in the greatest nation in the world. There are 330 million. people in this country. And they're 535 who get to have some say in the direction of the country. That's an awesome, awesome responsibility. And I don't take it for granted any day. I think it's the most remarkable thing. It's like winning the lottery of lotteries. And I loved the idea of running for politics and getting to say my views and getting to have an impact. I wish more people would just talk about some of the positives of politics, because I think we're so afraid that sometimes of saying it and young people, it's almost like they're embarrassed about wanting to do stuff in politics. I mean, this is a phenomenal country. It's still the most open country in the world. And for me, it was exhilarating to say, look, some person, a son, a immigrant can have an impact and people care. And so it's something that I always wanted to do afterwards. But I realized I had a long way to go because I had a pretty poor showing. And so then I said, OK, what are the things I got to improve? I got to figure out how to be more tied in the community. You got to get some experience. You got to be able to raise money. And that's the reality of politics these days. I didn't really do that in my first campaign. And then I, 10 years later, after I felt I had developed all of that, there was a new district that came out and I thought I'd be a good person to represent Silicon Valley District and ran. And lost a second time, came close, 52-48, but lost a second time.",
