    "turn_text": "You know, I think that you are as close to being 100% right as one can be with an answer that complicated. I like to remind people that Dr. King wrote that letter from jail. So there was a consequence to his belief in the unjustness of that law. The other thing that, so too for your grandfather. I mean, Jim Clyburn, you know, met his late wife, Emily, in jail. So the consequence of the law, they were willing to accept to change it. And the other thing that just floors me about that letter from Birmingham Jail, all the references to literature and history and scripture with no library, just whatever was in his head, he was able to write Um, and that letter, you correct me if I'm wrong, that letter was not written to his political opponents. That letter was written to people that were supposed to be his friends. Um, and it is a very challenging, I would encourage people to, to read that will be right back with more of the Tragati podcast.",
