        "text": "Public trust in democratic processes depends on perceived fairness and mutual respect in debate.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "Ideological bias is inherently problematic when it leads to dehumanization or dismissal of opposing viewpoints.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "Engaging in genuine dialogue requires suspending assumptions of intellectual or moral superiority.",
        "confidence": 0.86
      },
      {
        "text": "Civic values like listening and persuasion are more important than winning arguments ideologically.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      },
      {
        "text": "People generally recognize when discourse lacks respect even if they cannot articulate why.",
        "confidence": 0.83
      },
      {
        "text": "The current state of public discourse reflects deeper societal fractures related to identity and power.",
