    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Assert / Elaborate"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 89151,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/9/89151.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 46,
    "turn_text": "All right, this is a hard question. I actually posed it when I was on the House Intel Committee to some of the media titans. Those are smart lawyers. They were smart enough not to try to answer it, but I do not. You and I are talking on a Monday. I do not see the value in me telling people that we're talking on a Thursday. I just, it's wrong, it's inaccurate. I don't know how it benefits people. Where do you think the line is, if at all, between free speech and propagating intentionally misinformation?",
